            "The internet works fast.",
            "It's not that the internet doesn't work."
          ],
          "answer": 2,
          "explanation": "Çalışmıyor — “doesn't work,” değil — the second “not.” It works, but with a catch."
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "prompt": "Gelmeyeceğim.",
          "say": "Gelmeyeceğim.",
          "options": [
            "I won't come.",
            "It's not that I won't come.",
            "I'll come."
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "There's one “not” here, and the tail -im sits on the verb. That's just “I won't come.”"
        },
        {
          "id": "d",
          "prompt": "Anlamıyor değiliz.",
          "say": "Anlamıyor değiliz.",
          "options": [
            "It's not that we don't understand.",
            "We don't understand.",
            "It's not that you all don't understand."
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Değiliz means “we.” Two “nots” — so it's “it's not that we don't understand.”"
        }
      ]
